* TR10 RX_LNA -- narrowband common-source LNA with continuous AGC.
*
* Engineering example.  Signal path is PDK MOS; the tank is ideal L/C with a
* configurable Q and the AGC bias is an ideal voltage source.
*
* Ports: in out vdd vss agc
*   in   50 ohm RF input, AC coupled to the gate
*   out  source-follower output, DC ~2.66 V, AC couple before the balun
*   agc  0..5 V -> gate bias 0.77..1.35 V -> drain current 60 uA..2 mA
*        -> voltage gain ~1..20 dB
*
* The source is grounded.  A single-ended common-source stage cannot put its
* source on an ideal current sink: the source node then floats at AC, the
* gate-source voltage stays ~0 and gm collapses.  AGC therefore varies the
* gate bias, not a tail current.
*
* Default tank is 1 MHz: L=15.9 uH, C=1.59 nF, Rp=2.0 kohm (Q=20).
* L scales as 1/fc and C is recomputed so the tank stays at fc.
*
* NOTE: rgval=1 on every analog MOS.  rgval=0 is clamped to 1e-12 ohm by
* ngspice and the DC operating point goes singular.
.subckt RX_LNA in out vdd vss agc
.param fc=1e6 q=20
.param wc = 2*3.141592653589793*fc
.param Lval = 15.9u*1e6/fc
.param Cval = 1/(wc*wc*Lval)
.param Rp = q*wc*Lval

* 50 ohm input termination and AC coupling
Rterm in vss 50
Cin in g 100n

* AGC: gate bias 0.77 V (60 uA) .. 1.35 V (2 mA), bypassed to AC ground
Bv vg vss V = {0.77 + 0.116*v(agc)}
Rg vg g 100k

* common-source gain stage, grounded source
X1 d g vss vss NMOS_nf w=200u l=1u nf=10 rgval=1

* ideal parallel tank at fc
Lt d vdd {Lval}
Ct d vdd {Cval}
Rp d vdd {Rp}

* source-follower buffer, 4 mA
X2 vdd d out vss NMOS_nf w=200u l=1u nf=10 rgval=1
Ibuf out vss dc 4m
.ends RX_LNA
